WEBVTT

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.530
kikoeru ka kikoeru darou

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.530
<i>Can you hear it? I'm sure you can...</i>

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.360
harukana todoroki

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:14.360
<i>...that faraway roar!</i>

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.530
yami no naka kokoro yusaburu

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.530
<i>Your soul trembles in the darkness</i>

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.700
mezame hajimaru

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.700
<i>as it begins to awaken</i>

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.750
daichi wari sosoritatsu sugata

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.750
<i>A towering figure shatters the earth</i>

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
seigi no akashi ka

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>Is it the symbol of justice?</i>

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.010
densetsu no kyojin no chikara

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:33.010
<i>The legendary giant's power</i>

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.970
ginga kirisaku

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.970
<i>will tear through the galaxy!</i>

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.220
otakebi ga denkou sekka no

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.220
<i>Our war cry will summon</i>

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.060
ichigeki wo yobu

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:42.060
<i>a flash of lightning!</i>

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.100
furueru na hitomi korase yo

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.100
<i>Have no fear, focus your eyes on...</i>

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.480
fukkatsu no toki

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.480
<i>the moment of resurrection!</i>

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.240
hito yo inochi yo hajimari wo miru

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.240
<i>Mankind and all life witness it begin</i>

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:03.160
<i>Space Runaway ldeon, Ideon</i>

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:10.170
<i>Space Runaway Ideon, Ideon</i>

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.810
It has been possible to travel from
one galaxy to another for 50 years.

00:01:35.530 --> 00:01:40.910
2.7 million light years away from
 Earth in the Andromeda Galaxy,

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:44.660
the star system A7 contains an Earth-like planet.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.210
On that planet, Solo,

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:53.920
Earthlings have carried out first contact
with an alien race known as the Buff Clan.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:12.900
<b>The Trembling Earth</b>

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:22.240
I wonder if everyone got killed in New Lopia too...

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.370
I guess... It's the same as here.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.290
Anyone who didn't evacuate to the
second excavation site is probably dead.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.460
I wonder if my Mom and Dad...

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:38.800
...ended up like your Dad.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.930
That can't be! They must have made it!

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:41.760
Let's go.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.530
Those were aliens?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.860
If it's for Lady Karala's sake...

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:04.830
An alien?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.460
Oh, it's just a girl. Go inside, it's dangerous out here.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.840
If we could just install a missile or two...

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:21.300
That's better than not having any.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.180
What's this?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.390
Are there any injured people here?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.860
Are you sure this is all of it?

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.940
That's it for the dynamometer blueprints.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.200
I don't get it. If this was built by the aliens
 of Logo Dau, why did they bury it here?

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.200
You, over there!

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.960
Non-authorized personnel should stay away from here.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.000
Are you one of the third generation immigrants?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.550
Please stay near the entrance.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.390
There's an Ideon Gauge in here too!

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.180
Yeah.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:07.600
Ideon?

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:10.180
Ide...

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.100
Lady Karala.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.060
Mayaya.

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.520
I'm very sorry.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.980
We have to return immediately.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.780
We can't. The aliens here know of the Ide.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:22.940
The Ide?

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:26.200
They call it "Ideon." I want to investigate more.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:27.530
Yes.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.870
Just transmit a position signal.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.370
Yes.

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.170
I wonder if he wants milk.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.090
Here, it's a nipple.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:46.760
There, there, Lou. I've brought you some milk.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.180
Here.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:56.100
Hey, Lotta. About New Lopia...

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.190
Don't talk about it. We've got little kids here.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.150
Oh, sorry. Everyone's fine.

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.320
This is the third one.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.160
What could it be?

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:10.490
It's appeared again?

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.950
There has to be something I can do too!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.120
Deck, now's not the time.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.160
But New Lopia was just destroyed...

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.040
Shut up!

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.500
You don't know how I feel!

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:21.550
Bes.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:22.300
What is it?

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:26.470
Can't the military give us a little
more assistance for our research?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.720
Just look at our current situation here.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.260
Do you think we have time for academic research?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.720
If we knew the cause of these tremors,

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.640
we might be able to find out if
they're related to the Ideon Gauge.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.730
Plus, we might be able to learn
the full capabilities of this ship.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:43.070
You "might be able"?

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:46.400
While we're trying to confirm that possibility,
what if we get attacked by the enemy?

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.070
Bes.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:47.700
What?

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.070
As I thought, there's a signal that
resembles the enemy's pattern.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:51.700
Do you get it now?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:52.030
Huh?

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.000
An enemy spy might have snuck aboard.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.000
No way.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.790
Do you think the enemy is
wearing a nameplate or something?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:02.090
Can we pursue him?

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.750
The signal's constantly changing.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.300
I'll find him.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.770
Mayaya's signal is being transmitted
from alien point PK.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:24.570
What should we do, Gije?

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.280
Rescue Lady Karala, of course.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.490
We're low on resources. Should
we ask Sir Abadede for assistance?

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.620
As if we could do something like that.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.450
We're responsible for Lady Karala's disappearance.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:37.660
Is there a way to rescue her?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:38.200
There is.

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:41.960
I would like to recruit men for a suicide
 squad for the purpose of rescuing Lady Karala.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.670
There is no guarantee you'll make it back alive.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.050
A suicide squad?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.180
Hey, Gije.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.720
In return, if this mission is successful,

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:55.890
you may even reach the desired rank of Sabia.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.390
Sabia?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.390
That's a nearly unattainable rank, what do we do?

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:02.940
You're a reckless youth, Zudaka.

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:07.360
Damae? Why would someone as
cautious as you volunteer?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.610
My body's starting get too old for
this kind of work. That's why...

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:17.080
I see. You want to make a name for
yourself one last time for your daughter.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.160
Do your best!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.620
Sir. Thank you very much.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:30.170
This is an antimatter engine, right?

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:30.590
Yeah.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.300
Hold it right there. Turn around slowly.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.720
Is that you, Karala?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:41.770
Karala Ajiba...

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.230
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:07:45.230 --> 00:07:46.360
What...?

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:50.990
Jordan Bes!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.030
Karala... Why'd she shoot him?

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:56.570
Why!?

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.580
Why... why...

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:00.040
Mayaya, stop.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.040
That man isn't dead. He's just unconscious.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.880
Who are you two? Where are
you from? Are you Earthlings?

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.010
If not, then what the hell are you?

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.720
We're Earthlings. We're Earthlings too.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:17.760
Earthlings?

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.100
The name of our people is the Buff Clan.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:22.730
I'm a Buff Clan woman.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.740
Bring the missile control panel near the cockpit.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:37.570
Got it.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.490
How's it going in the cockpit?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:44.500
If there are people as talented as Cosmo around,
 send someone here, even if it's just a kid!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.590
We're just as shorthanded, and we've
got two more of these things to go!

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:54.470
Dammit, I even have to attach this seat
on my own so I can fight the enemies.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.550
I see you, I see you! Cosmo, how ya doin'?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.020
Deck! What are you doing?!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.690
There was a spare communication
unit left, so I borrowed it. Well?

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:06.810
Whaddya mean, "Well?"

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.400
Have you figured out everything
about that machine yet?

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:11.980
There's no way I could do that this quickly!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.820
Listen. Go ask Sheryl to give me
all the documents on this...

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:21.330
Enemies! It's the enemy!

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.200
But I don't know anything yet...
Cosmo, the enemy!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:27.670
Shit.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.090
Damn it!

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.760
Just watch. I can do this... GO!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.390
How do we turn this into a fighter?

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.060
Press the first two buttons on the right.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:49.520
Roger.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:56.780
Fire the missiles! Don't let them escape!

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.660
We've started to move too! Um, what should we do?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.540
We're launching too, alright?

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:13.170
Good, it looks like we can dock. Let's go!

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:16.420
Take care of it, Cosmo. The enemy's coming!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.430
All right! We've docked!

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:31.730
We'd be better off fighting separated, Cosmo!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.580
The smaller one is a radio transmitter, right?

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:48.200
Yes.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:53.330
I can't believe it... you two are aliens.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.800
When I hear of aliens I think of...

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:01.010
Four hands, six legs... Ugly monsters with
muddled skin, or so you thought.

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:02.470
True.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.640
I think you're a wonderful man, Bes.

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:11.980
Well, you're quite beautiful yourself, but I'm
going to confine you as prisoners now. OK?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.230
You've got no choice, right?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.280
It's the enemy!

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.490
Take this!

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:25.950
The enemy is here?!

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.040
What are your instructions?

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.540
"Instructions?"

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.290
Counter their attack by any means possible!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:31.960
Sir!

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:33.500
Where's Bes?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:41.970
Bastard!

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.430
Is that the place where the signal vanished?

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.020
Yes.

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:52.440
Alright, Zudaka. We don't know
what's in there, so be prepared.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.000
Land on the left terrace!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:18.290
It's the enemy!

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.300
Zudaka, find Lady Karala no matter what.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:26.800
Sir!

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:38.560
Damned Mayaya, send us a signal!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:44.240
Do you know where the Buff Clan women are? Answer!

00:12:44.700 --> 00:12:45.860
B-Buff Clan?

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:49.910
Tell me! This isn't just a threat!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.870
If you're not going to talk...

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:12.770
A barrier?! They've developed such technology?

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:18.100
Zudaka... I let you die in vain...

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.110
We're safe. Thank goodness.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:25.900
Who the hell are you?

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.780
I've got to make some fundamental
changes in my strategy.

00:13:33.950 --> 00:13:36.250
Yeah! Cosmo, you can turn around now.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.290
Are you getting used to it?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.210
Yeah, this is much better than sitting in a cockpit.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:48.380
They're fighters. Target them with all our missiles!

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:13.580
Tell all units to retreat!

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.370
The enemies are retreating.

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:16.750
They retreated?!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.750
What are you aiming at?

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:28.510
It should have been a direct hit!

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.310
Okay! I'm gonna crush you!

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.690
We were only able to shoot down 2 of them...

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.110
It's odd, isn't it?

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:46.230
What is?

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:48.530
Don't you think their strategy was strange?

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:51.820
It wasn't a battle to wipe us out completely.

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.160
True.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:57.830
What if this was just a diversion,
and they have some other objective in mind?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:58.620
Objective?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.840
For example... They could have an
interest in this artifact too.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.210
That's possible.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.010
It doesn't look like they're separating this time. Why?

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.550
Seriously. What's going on, Sheryl?

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.890
Get the wounded soldiers treated!

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:46.170
Transmit a message to Gije.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.750
Inform him that I'll be arriving soon.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:52.880
The search for the Ide has brought
about contact with aliens, huh?

00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:56.890
That Gije drew the short straw this time.

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.310
How'd the weapons installation go?

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:04.100
I asked an army engineer to do it.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.980
So, don't you have a map of the passages
in this thing after it becomes Ideon?

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:10.650
Why would we? Here's some food.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.070
Yeah, alright.

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.870
Hey, send the guy who was
adjusting this machine up here.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.500
There's nobody on the spaceship's bridge right now.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.000
They're busy trying to escape from here using
 that thing. Cosmo, what are you going to do?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.000
Spaceship?

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.710
Yeah. The thing that's buried is a spaceship.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.760
Also, they call the machine
you're riding in the Ideo Delta.

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.220
Who cares what's it called?!
Tell them to bring me missiles!

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:43.940
We know that this spaceship has an antimatter
engine from our investigations thus far, but...

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:49.940
there's something else in the central part of
the structure that we haven't identified yet.

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.570
Huh? You don't know what it is?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:58.280
We tried to find clues for deciphering the language
 of the Sixth Civilization from the computers,

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:04.040
but they were full of complex symbols, and
the only word we could understand was "Ideon."

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.000
Joliver, how's the engine coming?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.790
I can make it work, but it'll take some time.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.710
Get this thing airborne any way you can, all right?

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:13.510
Roger.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:18.340
If worst comes to worst, we'll have to get out
of this cave using the antimatter engine.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.350
That's right.

00:17:20.350 --> 00:17:22.970
However, we've got to break through the earth.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:26.310
That might render the spaceship unusable.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:28.270
In any case, it's worth a try.

00:17:28.600 --> 00:17:30.230
Alright, let's get prepared.

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.530
It seems that you failed to rescue Lady Karala.

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:42.030
Sir. Now that it's come to this, we're going to
atone and detonate ourselves at the enemy base.

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:46.500
Don't be so hasty. A Samurai shouldn't simply
 rush to his death, are you giving up already?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.330
But then, the responsibility...

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.090
If you stay alive, you still have
a chance to bring Lady Karala back.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:55.050
Was that not the mission appointed to you?

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:59.180
This is no longer a problem you can handle alone.

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.220
Yes, sir.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:13.480
It's good that the Southern Cross' Black
Hole Galaxy Transmitter survived.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:16.070
Yeah, but the adjustments will take time.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.370
Good, after this will be the rations.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.660
We've brought all the missiles from Block 23.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.120
Go!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:30.710
Yay!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.420
We don't need toys. Just bring food or weapons.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.550
We've got schoolbooks too!

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.970
At any rate, leaving right away might be impossible...

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:46.100
That can't be!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:49.310
We need to launch tonight and escape from Solo.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:55.110
I don't want to see these Sixth Civilization
relics get destroyed by ignorant enemies.

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:57.820
Soldiers like you can't comprehend their value!

00:18:58.360 --> 00:18:59.280
Sheryl...

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:14.130
Damned aliens... I'm going to bring back
Lady Karala no matter what it takes.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.920
Evacuate! Everyone, evacuate!

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:21.970
Protect the civilians at the entrance!

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.840
Hurry inside!

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:27.350
Are they coming?

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.120
This thing's tough, but how long will it last?

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:53.420
Cosmo! The enemy's aiming for the spaceship.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.380
Get down there! Get down there!

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:56.340
I know!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.550
Kasha, you just handle the missile controls.

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.940
They're trying to get to the spaceship, huh?

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:16.810
Take this!

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.700
It's just a machine, so there should
be a weak point somewhere.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:25.780
There?

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:30.790
They got us?

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:31.870
A direct hit?

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.050
Get down!

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.600
I'm scared!

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:54.980
Lady Karala...

00:20:59.060 --> 00:21:01.900
This is an earthquake, not an explosion.

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.690
The Ideon Gauge...

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:24.050
What the...

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:37.810
The place where the spaceship is...

00:21:58.210 --> 00:21:59.080
It's moving!

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:00.920
The spaceship!

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.800
Joliver! You got the main engine working?

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.760
I don't know. We're still adjusting it.

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:17.940
What? Then, how did this ship move?

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:21.020
Sheryl, what are you hiding from us?

00:22:22.770 --> 00:22:26.320
I'm not hiding anything. I told you everything.

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.490
Something came out from the earth... a spaceship!?

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:31.990
What?

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:36.080
Why from beneath the earth of all places!?

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:56.770
<i>Hoping to escape, the people take refuge in the
spaceship left behind by the Sixth Civilization.</i>

00:22:57.430 --> 00:23:03.480
<i>However, Cosmo, left behind with the Ideon,
is trapped by the Buff Clan's surprise attack.</i>

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:09.070
<i>Can the spaceship that started running on its
 own power save the Ideon from destruction?</i>

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:14.990
<i>Next time on Legendary Giant
Ideon: "Escape from Planet Solo."</i>

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:17.700
<b>Escape from Planet Solo</b>

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:35.720
tatta hitotsu no hoshi ni suterare

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:35.720
<i>I've been abandoned merely by one world</i>

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:43.060
owarinai tabi kimi to ayumu to

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:43.060
<i>As I walk this endless journey together with you</i>

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:48.610
itsukushimi futo wakeatte

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:48.610
<i>We unexpectedly share our affection</i>

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:55.990
kizu wo nameau douke shibai

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:55.990
<i>Feeling sympathy for each other in this farcical play</i>

00:23:56.330 --> 00:24:02.080
kosumosu sora wo kakenukete

00:23:56.330 --> 00:24:02.080
<i>Traveling through the skies of cosmos</i>

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:08.670
inori wo ima kimi no moto e

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:08.670
<i>I'll send a prayer your way</i>

